 36CA    1H(37CA,D):XUNDL-3            2021LA04                           202208
 36CA c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2021La04:                          
 36CA2c  Phys Rev C 103, 055809 (2022)                                          
 36CA c  Compiled by J. Chen (FRIB, MSU), July 6, 2022                          
 36CA c  2021La04: E=48 MeV/nucleon radioactive {+37}Ca beam was produced at    
 36CA2c  GANIL in fragmentation of a 95 MeV/nucleon {+40}Ca primary beam on a   
 36CA3c  2mm {+9}Be production target, and separated by the LISE3 spectrometer. 
 36CA4c  Reaction target was the liquid hydrogen target CRYPTA. Charged         
 36CA5c  particles were detected with the MUST2 detector array of six telescopes
 36CA6c  each consisting of a double-sided silicon strip detector (DSSD) backed 
 36CA7c  by sixteen 4cm thick CsI detectors. Measured excitation functions,     
 36CA8c  proton-deuteron angular correlations. Deduced proton resonance levels, 
 36CA9c  proton branching ratios. Calculated spectroscopic factors, proton and  
 36CAac  |g widths, resonance strengths, reaction rate of astrophysical         
 36CAbc  {+35}K(p,|g) reaction. Discussed astrophysical implications.           
 36CA cL $S(p)({+36}Ca)=2570 {I40} (2021Wa16)                                   
